// Local, machine-specific signing config — copy this file to Local.xcconfig (gitignored) and
// fill in your own team ID. Not committed because a Development Team ID is tied to your Apple
// ID, not the project.
//
// Find your team ID: Xcode > Settings > Accounts, select your Apple ID, select the team under
// it (a personal/free account shows as "<Your Name> (Personal Team)"), then "Manage Certificates"
// or hover/click the team row — the ID is the 10-character alphanumeric string shown there.
// It also appears in Signing & Capabilities after you pick a team there once.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID

// Base URL of the backing-track API.
//
// Debug builds already default to http://localhost:5198 (set in project.yml) so the simulator
// works against a local `dotnet run` with no setup. Set this for Release / on-device builds to
// point at the Pi — its Tailscale MagicDNS HTTPS name, which `tailscale serve` proxies to the API
// on port 5080 (scripts/pi-bootstrap.sh, ADR 0042). No port in the URL.
//
// The $() is a required Xcode idiom: an xcconfig treats // as a start-of-comment, so the two
// slashes in a URL scheme have to be separated by an empty $() expansion or everything from
// http:// onwards is silently dropped.
//
// API_BASE_URL = https:/$()/<your-pi>.<your-tailnet>.ts.net
